== Careers in STEM day
*Wednesday 25#super[th] March 2026*

= Computer Science after College

== Aims
We're going to be comparing some future options relating to Comp Sci:
- #text(orange)[Academic University Courses]#pause
- #text(blue)[Professional & Technical university Courses]#pause
- #text(green)[Degree Apprenticeships]

to make sure you can make an informed decision about what to do after college.

This will also include transferable skills for researching future options!

== Types of University Courses
There's a lot of courses called 'Computer Science' out there.

They each provide unique experiences, but the course content on them can vary wildly!

Broadly, courses are either more #text(orange)[academic] or more #text(blue)[practical].

How do you tell the difference? What do they offer you?

== #text(orange)[Academic University Courses]
- Higher grade requirements (usually above #bold[BBB]) #pause
- Often require Maths A-level \ (sometimes other maths/science subject requirements)#pause
- Broad range of topics looked at in a deep #text(orange)[mathematical] way#pause
- Traditional computer science topics \ (e.g. Algorithms, Discrete Mathematics, Computer Architecture, Computation and Complexity theory)

== #text(orange)[Academic University Courses]
#text(21pt)[#grid(columns:(1fr,1fr),
[
  *Advantages*
  #uncover("1-")[
    - Likely to have a higher reputation amongst employers.
    - Better future academia/research options (Masters / PhD)
  ]
  #uncover("3-")[
    - Teaches you a broad range of topics which you could apply in the future
  ]
  #uncover("5-")[
    - Russell group unis often have excellent industry links
  ]
  #uncover("7-")[
    - Possibility of paid work experience
  ]
],[
  *Disadvantages*
  #uncover("2-")[
    - Stricter entry requirements
  ]
  #uncover("4-")[
    - Relatively less practical experience
  ]
  #uncover("6-")[
    - Takes longer before you specialise in one area
  ]
])]

== #text(blue)[Practical University Courses]
- Usually lower entry requirements, often UCAS points #pause
- Courses will be much more practical based\ eg. learning specific languages or web tools#pause
- Assessments more heavily weighted towards \ practical exercises/reports#pause
- Often also a focus on the Business/IT side of the commercial sector

== #text(blue)[Practical University Courses]
#text(21pt)[#grid(columns:(1fr,1fr),
[
  *Advantages*
  #uncover("1-")[
    - Easier to get/meet an offer
    - Sometimes bursaries for high A-level grades
  ]
  #uncover("3-")[
    - Will gain practical skills more directly relevant to particular industries
  ]
  #uncover("5-")[
    - More personal support
  ]
  
],[
  *Disadvantages*
  #uncover("2-")[
    - Sometimes lower reputation
  ]
  #uncover("4-")[
    - Topics are covered in less depth
  ]
  #uncover("6-")[
    - Some jobs/projects require more understanding \ (eg. compiler design)
  ]
])]

